Subject: Using lapply to iterate over a list of aesthetic mappings
Message-ID: <LGi_hTMqLwk.btDUcb_VAgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/LGi_hTMqLwk/m/btDUcb_VAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all, if we take the iris data.frame:
data(iris)

I wish to map Sepal.Length to x, and Sepal.Width to y, and I would like to create three more plots by iterating over the remaining variables in the data.frame for the colour aesthetic. I've tried to do this by creating a list of plots using lapply as shown below, but for some reason, the colours take on a single value for each plot. Could someone please guide me as to where I'm going wrong?

Many thanks
Hefin

library(ggplot2)

plots <- lapply(colnames(iris)[3:5], function(i){
  ggplot(iris, aes(Sepal.Length, Sepal.Width, col = i)) + geom_point()
})

plots

From u373beb702917b8b5 at groups.google.com  Mon May 15 15:08:22 2017
From: u373beb702917b8b5 at groups.google.com (Ista Zahn)
Date: Mon, 15 May 2017 15:08:22 +0000
Subject: Re: Using lapply to iterate over a list of aesthetic mappings
Message-ID: <LGi_hTMqLwk.CPWX_0y4BAAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <LGi_hTMqLwk.btDUcb_VAgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <LGi_hTMqLwk.btDUcb_VAgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/LGi_hTMqLwk/m/CPWX_0y4BAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

colnames gives you column names as a character vector, so you'll need
something like

plots <- lapply(colnames(iris)[3:5], function(i){

  ggplot(iris, aes_string("Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width", col = i)) +
geom_point()
})

Best,
Ista

